<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">White Christmas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">written c. 1940; first performed 25 December <a href="/years/1941">1941</a>; recorded 29 May <a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;White <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas">Christmas</a>&quot; was written by Irving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> for the 1942 musical film Holiday Inn. Accounts differ as to when and where he wrote it. One story is that he wrote it in 1940 in warm La Quinta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, while staying at the La Quinta Hotel, a retreat favoured by Hollywood; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arizona">Arizona</a> Biltmore also claims the song was written there.</p></div>
